BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-1tz9nux@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260919T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260919T210000
SUMMARY:Unsettled: The Search Between Wandering & Belonging
DESCRIPTION:After multiple sold-out seasons across Australia and a 5-star r
 eview at Fringe World Perth \, Unsettled: The Search Between Wandering & B
 elonging returns to the Gold Coast\, for a special one-night performance. 
 One woman. One suitcase. Too many existential crisis. What happens when ho
 me is no longer a place you can find on a map? Unsettled: The Search Betwe
 en Wandering & Belonging is a fearless\, funny\, and deeply moving one-wom
 an show about chasing dreams\, getting lost along the way\, and building a
  new life from scratch. With humour and intimate honesty\, Agustina takes 
 you on a wild ride through the heartbreak\, comedy\, and chaos of living a
 broad. Vulnerable\, hilarious\, and fiercely alive\, Unsettled invites you
  to feel seen\, laugh\, cry\, and maybe even find a piece of yourself alon
 g the way. What began as a street performance in Port Douglas has evolved 
 into a multi-city\, sold-out show \, touring Magnetic Island\, Airlie Beac
 h\, Noosa\, Byron Bay\, Gold Coast\, Margaret River\, and successful sell 
 out seasons at Adelaide Fringe\, Fringe World Perth\, Sydney Fringe & Melb
 ourne Fringe. Following a successful Byron Bay season\, with nine performa
 nces and multiple sold-out nights\, Unsettled heads just up the coast to G
 old Coast. After previously appearing at Miami Marketta as part of HOLA Ma
 rketta the Winter Latin Festival \, the show returns for a special standal
 one performance\, bringing its playful storytelling to new audiences. This
  time\, experience it in a cozy\, intimate venue\, perfect for getting up 
 close and personal with the story. ⚠️Limited capacity. One night only.
  Don’t miss out 😏 ⏰ Doors open 6PM Show 7PM - 9PM 📌 Miami Market
 ta\, Mona Lisa's Lair More than just a show! Enjoy live music before the p
 erformance \, grab a drink and settle in for the evening. Following the sh
 ow\, there will be a Q&A and informal discussion with Agustina \, explorin
 g and unpacking some of the themes at the heart of Unsettled . Come for th
 e story. Stay for the conversation
LOCATION:Miami Marketta
URL:https://www.miamimarketta.com/ticketed-events/unsettled
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-54mo77@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260924T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260924T210000
SUMMARY:ADALITA (GOLD COAST)
DESCRIPTION:Released in 2011\, Adalita’s self-titled debut marked the beg
 inning of her remarkable solo journey. Raw\, intimate\, and emotionally fe
 arless\, it struck a deep chord with listeners and remains one of the most
  beloved and influential Australian releases of its time. To mark its fift
 eenth anniversary\, Adalita reunites with original collaborator JP Shilo t
 o perform the album in full\, revisiting the songs that first began this e
 xtraordinary chapter. Coinciding with the tour\, Adalita will also be reis
 sued on vinyl through Mushroom Music\, bringing a long out-of-print favour
 ite back to fans fifteen years on. Don’t miss these special shows. Suppo
 rted by JP Shilo and more. WILL SELL OUT / GET IN EARLY! Doors at 7pm. El 
 Ranchero back deck/bar and Spanish Girl Food Co will be open from 6pm for 
 preshow dinner and drinks. ADALITA Mo's Desert Clubhouse (GOLD COAST) Thur
 sday 24 September 2026 // 7pm doors $40+BF online GA or $50 door if still 
 available // 18+ Mo's is Burleigh Heads' most loved music venue\, licensed
  bars\, creative studios and cultural hub. The Warehouse & El Ranchero bot
 h boast epic bar menus\, cocktails and craft beers. Mo's is a fully licens
 ed venue\, all guests are required to show ID on entry. Tickets will only 
 be refunded through event cancellation or production of a medical certific
 ate within 24hrs of show doors.
LOCATION:Mo's Desert Clubhouse
URL:https://tickets.oztix.com.au/outlet/event/87e616a3-49f2-4b59-9467-488bb
 d20d580
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-nkt6i@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260925T053000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260925T073000
SUMMARY:ANH DO
DESCRIPTION:Anh Do’s bestselling book The Happiest Refugee has made reade
 rs laugh and cry\, and was described by Russell Crowe as 'the most surpris
 ing and inspiring read I have had in years.' Anh’s stage show takes it a
  step further\, combining stand-up comedy with real life stories\, photos 
 and filmed pieces to retell his amazing story. When one of Australia’s m
 ost talented comedians delves deep into his own life’s joys and sorrows\
 , the result is an unforgettable night at the theatre that leaves an audie
 nce uplifted and quite simply experiencing... happiness. 'Irrepressible go
 od humour\, infectious energy and bright optimism' The Sydney Morning Hera
 ld 'The happiest audience experience I have ever had' …ArtsHub 'Two thum
 bs\, five stars\, show of the season' The Music
LOCATION:The Showroom\, 2 Wharf st\, Tweed Heads\, NSW 2486
URL:https://twintowns.com.au/events/anh-do/
END:VEVENT
