 n: center\; } @media (max-width: 30rem) { .tje-case-card .card-poster { fo
 nt-size: 2.3rem\; } } ⚖️ Watch drama | 🗳️ Cast a vote | 🕵️ C
 rack the case ⭐ You've been called for jury duty. Step into a thrilling 
 courtroom drama where the audience is the jury. Listen to testimonies\, an
 alyze evidence\, and ultimately decide… guilty or not guilty? It's not t
 heatre you watch. It's justice you deliver. The Million Dollar Murder Insp
 ired by true events\, this gripping courtroom drama pulls you into a world
  where greed\, passion\, and revenge collide — and where the line betwee
 n victim and villain is razor-thin. The accused stands in the dock\, but i
 s this a cold-blooded killer\, or a pawn in a far more dangerous game? No 
 DNA evidence. A tangled web of desire and betrayal. And a divorce worth mi
 llions. Every witness has a reason to lie. Every motive points somewhere d
 ifferent. Can you untangle the truth before the verdict is cast? 🚩 This
  experience includes themes of murder and violent death\, domestic violenc
 e\, emotional manipulation. There is a detailed discussion of a homicide. 
 The performance contains moments of intense emotional conflict. Highlights
  🤩 Enjoy a live theatre courtroom drama where you decide the final verd
 ict 🫵 Vote during key moments - your decisions shape hidden angles in t
 he case\, making every show different! 🕵️‍♂️ Dissect witness te
 stimonies\, unpack evidence\, and weigh every argument 🎢 A high-stakes 
 case full of twists - more turns than a rollercoaster\, and a verdict only
  you can deliver How it works 1 Take your seat Arrive 30 min early. Doors 
 close at show time — late entry is not permitted. 2 Hear the case Track 
 every testimony\, spot the contradictions\, and vote at key moments to ste
 er the trial. 3 Deliver your verdict The jury speaks. Guilty or not guilty
  - the outcome rests entirely with you. Practical info ⏳ Duration 60 min
 utes Doors open 30 min before 📍 Venue Old Museum Brisbane 480 Gregory T
 errace\, Bowen Hills\, QLD 4006\, Australia 👤 Age 12+ Under 16s must be
  with an adult ♿ Accessibility Wheelchair accessible Wheelchair zone ava
 ilable ✨ Groups & Private Take the stand 30+ people or private show 🎁
  Gift card Send gift Gift memories to someone special Frequently asked que
 stions About the experience What is The Jury Experience and what can I exp
 ect? The Jury Experience is an immersive courtroom drama where you become 
 part of the story as a juror. Analyze testimonies\, cross-examinations\, a
 nd evidence to uncover the truth - your vote determines the accused's fate
 . How long does the experience last? The experience lasts approximately 1 
 hour. Will there be strobe lights? No\, there will not be any strobe light
 s. Are seats numbered? No\, seats are not assigned. Seating is first-come\
 , first-served within the zone you select when purchasing your ticket. Abo
 ut your tickets What are the different types of tickets available? A reser
 ve: Best visibility B reserve: Good visibility\, located on the sides C re
 serve: Fair visibility\, positioned further back D reserve: Fair visibilit
 y\, positioned further back behind C reserve Can I buy a ticket on site on
  the day of the event? Tickets cannot be purchased on site. All tickets mu
 st be purchased via the app or website (feverup.com) before arriving at th
 e event. Is it necessary to buy a ticket for my carer? Guests requiring as
 sistance are entitled to one free pass for their personal assistant/suppor
 t worker. Contact us to receive a voucher for a free carer ticket (based o
 n availability). The regular ticket must be shown together with the carer 
 ticket at entry. Can I change the date of my ticket? Are refunds allowed? 
 Subject to availability\, date/time changes are permitted up to 48 hours b
 efore the start time. Tickets are non-refundable except as required under 
 Australian Consumer Law. Can I transfer my tickets to another person? Yes\
 , tickets can be transferred to any other Fever account at no additional c
 ost via "Transfer tickets" in the Fever app. Where can I find my ticket? D
 o I need to print it out? Your ticket is in the "Tickets" section of the F
 ever app\, and also in your purchase confirmation email. You do not need t
 o print it - it's validated via the app on arrival. Access & venue Where d
 oes the show take place? The show takes place at The Old Museum\, 480 Greg
 ory Terrace\, Bowen Hills QLD 4006\, Australia. Does the experience take p
 lace indoors or outdoors? This experience takes place indoors in a heated/
 air-conditioned venue. Are food and drinks available on site for purchase?
  No\, food and drinks are not available for purchase on site. Are animals 
 allowed? Animals\, except assistance animals\, are not allowed. Is the ven
 ue accessible? Yes\, the event is held in an accessible venue. Accessible 
 seating is limited to Zone A and B only. Are there chairs available? Can I
  be seated during the experience? Yes\, this is a seated experience - seat
 ing is available for every guest. Will toilet facilities be available on s
 ite? Yes\, the venue has toilets\; on-site staff can direct you. Is there 
 parking on site? There is no dedicated venue parking\, but surrounding par
 king garages and limited street parking are available. Public transport or
  sustainable alternatives are recommended. Is cloakroom service available?
  Unfortunately\, this location does not have a cloakroom service. Can I ta
 ke photos or use my phone during the performance? Photos and videos can on
 ly be taken during the curtain call\, without flash. Phones must be in sil
 ent mode throughout the performance. Can I leave during the performance? W
 hat items are prohibited? Out of respect for the performers and the audien
 ce\, you may not leave your seat except in an emergency. Prohibited items 
 include smoking/vaping\, external alcohol\, hot food or drinks\, strong-sm
 elling food or glass\, audio recording devices\, drugs\, flammables\, torc
 hes\, lasers\, professional cameras\, promotional items\, and selfie stick
 s/tripods. Seating Map Murder #1 · The Million Dollar Murder
LOCATION:Fever Gold Coast\, Brisbane
URL:https://feverup.com/m/454336
END:VEVENT
