UID:goldcoast-1rzh30s@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260922T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260922T220000
SUMMARY:Strung Out (USA)
DESCRIPTION:US punk-metal mainstays Strung Out return to Australia this Sep
 tember to celebrate 30 years of their landmark album Suburban Teenage Wast
 eland Blues with a national run of headline shows. Originally released in 
 1996\, Suburban Teenage Wasteland Blues crammed 13 songs into 32 breakneck
  minutes and became a defining record for a generation of punk fans. From 
 the opening blast of “Firecracker” through to “Wrong Side of the Tra
 cks”\, the album’s mix of hook-heavy melodies and high-speed riffs sti
 ll hits just as hard today. Across ten albums and countless tours\, Strung
  Out have built a reputation as one of the most explosive live bands in pu
 nk rock – loud\, tight and direct\, with no throwbacks for the sake of i
 t and no wasted moments. This September\, Australian fans will hear Suburb
 an Teenage Wasteland Blues celebrated throughout the set\, alongside favou
 rites from across the band’s catalogue.
LOCATION:Miami Marketta (18+)
URL:https://www.miamimarketta.com/ticketed-events/strung-out
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goldcoast-fxx17p@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260922T210000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260922T230000
SUMMARY:BRIT BEAT MANIA
DESCRIPTION:Brit Beat Mania Brit Beat Mania - are widely regarded as one of
  Queensland’s best Pop Tribute Show Bands as they re-create the look\, t
 he sound and the magic that was The British Invasion. Their professionally
  presented show has been wowing audiences taking Baby Boomers back to thei
 r teens with an entertaining\, fun\, and interactive journey with songs fr
 om legendary artists such as Cliff Richard\, Herman’s Hermits\, The Holl
 ies\, Tom Jones\, Gerry & the Pacemakers\, The Beatles\, The Rolling Stone
 s and the many more who created the British Invasion. Tony Worsley Tony Wo
 rsley burst into the Australian recording industry in the early 60's and h
 is success was instantaneous. Hit after hit including "Missing You"\, "Rai
 ning in my Heart"\, "Knocking on Wood" as well as the Gold single "Velvet 
 Waters". In 1965 Tony toured nationally with The Kinks\, Manfred Mann and 
 The Honeycombs\, playing to packed houses of screaming fans. Tony has shar
 ed the stage with The Dave Clark Five\, The Seekers\, Johnny O'Keefe and J
 ohn Farnham. Tony’s onstage personality is full of charisma and his pres
 entation is as vibrant and polished now as that of any world-class enterta
 iner. So be ready to be entertained and transported back to the era that c
 hanged the musical landscape around the world that was The Sound of the 60
 ’s.
LOCATION:The Showroom\, 2 Wharf st\, Tweed Heads\, NSW 2486
URL:https://twintowns.com.au/events/brit-beat-mania/
END:VEVENT
